From: toktier maintainers
Subject: [PATCH] Add a `toktier` tokenizer backend (CPU, per-session reuse)

Adds `--tokenizer-backend toktier`, shaped like the `fastokens` branch:
the TokenizerManager wraps the tokenizer it has loaded, so encode calls
run on toktier's certified CPU route (ids equal to a from-scratch
reference encode), and the request's `session_id` (else `cache_salt`)
is bound around the tokenize call so a conversation's transcript is
served as a verified prefix append instead of a full re-encode.
`get_tokenizer` is not changed, so the scheduler, TP worker and
detokenizer processes keep the plain tokenizer they load. With the
adapter's process pool enabled (TOKTIER_SGLANG_SCHED_WORKERS > 0),
`_tokenize_texts` awaits the pool for plain text inputs instead of
encoding on the event loop's thread. No other code path changes.
The added code uses `nullcontext`, `logger` and `get_serving`, which
tokenizer_manager.py already imports in this baseline; the patch adds
no import of its own, so a port to another release should check that
the file still imports all three.
Requires `toktier >= 0.3.0` (toktier.integrations.sglang).
Baseline: sglang 0.5.19 (PyPI wheel).
